Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: v0.43 rolling core, round 1 (an id-less answer
 followed as before; logAsk on keep; no new named type)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RA-1: src/utils/lifecycle.ts's `post` now answers `{ id }` or nothing, so `follow` stops only where
the app didn't take the roll or couldn't be reached. A 202 whose body has no id is followed as the
base followed it again: `taken` hears undefined, the page asks after /rolls/undefined, and is told
`lost` once FOLLOW_FOR is up. Commit 15 had stopped there at once, so the roll stayed sending. The
real server always answers an id (seat-routes.ts:144). The review's differential harness, with
202 answers of {}, 0, 5, '' and { id: '' } added: 4,000 scenarios against a2332a2's follow, 0
diffs; at commit 15's follow, 1,026.

RA-2: logAsk keeps through the hook's private `keep`, so all nine log* share it, as R1.2.7 says.
`keep(kind, fields, at?)` takes the kind, which begins the id too (use-…, ask-…); the id's
Date.now() and ++uses, then `at`, in the same order, and the same key order (kind, id, the
fields, at). The eight `use` callers name their kind. Commit 15's message says nine; it was eight.

RA-3: src/utils/damage-modifiers.ts's FormulaScan type (new in commit 15) is gone: groupsOf's
scan is inferred, and readBracket and readSign each name the fields they read and write. Part
and FormulaGroup stay file-private, as at the base (a Phase 4 item).

L1 on this tree: jest, typegen and tsc, eslint and gates 1-12 all ok; next build ok.

